---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import '../styles/legal.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Website Terms"
  description="Terms that apply when you visit and use the Strictons website."
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-hero">
      <div class="legal-shell">
        <p class="legal-kicker">Legal</p>
        <h1>Website Terms</h1>
        <p class="legal-intro">
          These terms apply when you visit or use strictons.com. By using this
          website, you agree to them.
        </p>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated 24 September 2026</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-shell legal-content">
      <section>
        <h2>About this website</h2>
        <p>
          This website is operated by Strictons in New South Wales, Australia.
          It provides general information about Strictons, our hotel guides and
          opportunities for hotels and local businesses.
        </p>
        <p>
          These website terms do not replace any proposal, service agreement,
          order or other written agreement between you and Strictons. If there
          is an inconsistency, the specific written agreement will apply to the
          extent of the inconsistency.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Information on the website</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to keep the website accurate and useful, but its content is
          general information only. Details about availability, timing,
          inclusions, pricing, production and results may change and should be
          confirmed with us before you rely on them or make a decision.
        </p>
        <p>
          Images and examples may be illustrative. A reference to a hotel,
          business, product or service does not create an endorsement unless we
          clearly say otherwise.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You must not use the website to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>break any law or infringe another person’s rights;</li>
          <li>
            introduce malicious code, interfere with security or disrupt the
            website or its users;
          </li>
          <li>
            access or attempt to access non-public systems, accounts or data;
          </li>
          <li>
            scrape, copy or automatically extract substantial website content
            without our prior written permission; or
          </li>
          <li>misrepresent your identity or your relationship with us.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Unless stated otherwise, Strictons owns or licenses the website and
          its content, including its text, design, graphics, logos, images and
          other material. All rights are reserved.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may view the website and make a temporary copy for your personal
          or internal business use. You must not reproduce, adapt, publish,
          distribute, commercialise or otherwise use website content without our
          prior written permission, except as permitted by law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Trade marks and material belonging to third parties remain the
          property of their respective owners.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>
        <p>
          The website may link to or display services operated by others,
          including the Cal.com booking calendar and websites featured in guide
          examples. Those services have their own terms and privacy practices.
          We do not control them and are not responsible for their content,
          availability or operation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Availability and liability</h2>
        <p>
          We may change, suspend or withdraw any part of the website without
          notice. We do not promise that the website will always be available,
          uninterrupted, secure or free from errors or harmful components.
        </p>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Strictons excludes warranties
          and liability arising from your use of, or reliance on, this website.
          Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any right,
          guarantee or remedy that cannot lawfully be excluded, including under
          the Australian Consumer Law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle personal
          information collected through the website and our dealings with you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. The current version will
          be published here with its effective date. Your continued use of the
          website after an update means the updated terms apply to that use.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of New South Wales, Australia.
          You and Strictons submit to the non-exclusive jurisdiction of the
          courts of New South Wales and courts entitled to hear appeals from
          them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent to <a
            href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
